Subject: [PATCH] 551 B6 flip: LOT_SUM_AWARDS_PATH = true with both R10 guards
 (G-single, G-cover)

Path W v2 serves the vouched lot-award sum again, past the two guards B6
adopted (U4: both guards, P = v2+both 3,467). Tests re-pinned from "path W
off" to "served under BOTH" (production == switch-on twin; the switch-off
twin keeps the max election), a new 7202436-shape G-cover test, and the
production guard set pinned (true, true, true). /docs, OpenAPI, /v1/sql
notes, CHANGELOG and operations.md flip from "switched off" to "served
again since issue 551 B6". Built and reviewed by wf_f58c9b34-9a9 (three
lenses, a skeptic per finding, 11 of 12 surviving findings fixed; the
eighth-pin Rust fixtures are a U10 follow-up). Full package suite green
(2,456 passed, 0 failed, 34 ignored) on base 3df8748.

HELD OFF MAIN until the 10-21 post-chain flip window; re-gate on the
final base before it ships.

